I am doing this summary for posterity as I doubt that anyone else in the
digital UNIXverse will ever run across it.

The problem:

> On an alpha 2100 model 4/233
> DU 4.0D
> Firmware level v4.7-143
> OSF PALcode x1.45-12
> 
Error Messages occurred during boot 

> halted CPU 0
> 
> halt code = 7
> machine check while in PAL mode
> PC = 18958
> 
The solution:

The kernel that was being used was compiled on an AS 2100 model 5.  When
the kernel was compiled on a model 4 the problem went away.

Similarly a kernel compiled on an AS 2100 model 4 results in the
following error message when run on a Model 5:

halt code = 6
double error halt
PC = 18958

The generic kernel runs on either model.


