From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Sep 15 23:17:38 1998
From: Gary Menna <G.Menna () isu ! usyd ! edu ! au>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 1998 23:17:38 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: HSZ70 miscalculation
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078721911863

Hi All , 
Question : 
	After partitioning a raidset on a HSZ70 I noticed
	that the size given in 512k blocks does not match
	the size given in the brackets in MB . 	

Partition number        Size                  Starting Block     Used by

 1                  6280955 ( 3215.84 MB)            0            D100 
 2                 10469115 ( 5360.18 MB)      6280960            D101 
 3                  4186875 ( 2143.68 MB)     16750080            D102 
 4                  8375035 ( 4288.01 MB)     20936960            D103 
 5                  8793595 ( 4502.32 MB)     29312000            D104 
                    3771795 ( 1931.15 MB)     38105600            <free>

ANSWER : 
	After logging a call to Digitals CSS I was told that
	the HSZ70 uses the calculation for the good old
	"Marketing Megabyte" to work out the size in MBs .
	The Marketing MB is  blocks x 512 / 1,000,000 .
	This calculation is used in the dxdisk GUI with the 
	sliding bars used to partition disks as well . 

	ergo : 6280955 / 2048 = 3066   (the actual size of partition 1)

	6280955 x 512 = 3215848960   / 1,000,000 = 3215.84
	is the marketing MB . 

	That is why my 4.3 GB disks are only 4090MB
	and my 9 GB disks are only 8676 MB . 
	I was also told that my belief that there is 1024 bytes 
	to a KB and 1024 KB to a MB is just something that I
	had presumed , and does not necessarily mean its true . 


