From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Sep 09 17:05:07 1998
From: "Robert L. McMillin" <rlm () syseca-us ! com>
Date: Wed, 09 Sep 1998 17:05:07 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: DLT performance
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078721911738

It seems that the correct answers to my dilemma are that

(1) the drive's sustained throughput is closer to 5 MB/s
(2) higher rates obtain iff the disks are high-throughput RAID devices
(3) NetWorker Server Save & Restore can be used to increase throughput,
as it has better streaming capability than vdump.

Thanks to all who replied.

Incidentally, Dr. Tom Blinn indicated that Outlook/Exchange is
apparently mangling outbound e-mail. I'm using Netscape to hopefully
force this to a more reasonable condition. Sorry to anyone who was
inconvenienced by this.

