I posted the following question a few weeks ago:

>Fellow mangers:
>
>I know this question may be a little outside the scope, but I hope
>someone has some info.  I am looking for any kind of document showing
>Digital UNIX market share vs. other flavors of UNIX.  Also, any
>comparisons vs. NT would be nice also.
Thanks to:

Kraisit Vittinanon
Phil Farrell
JF Vibert
Stephen Spalding
Larry Clegg
William Beelen
Arun Sanghvi
Matthias Dolder
Dr. Ram Rao

I apologize for the delay in my response.  To part one of my question, I
received a few opinions about Digital UNIX has been taking market share
from SUN, HP, etc.  Some hard numbers came from Dr. Ram Rao of
Compaq in a report I have attached to this document (unixdoc.htm).  

In the UNIX vs. NT, all my responses pointed to
www.kirch.net/unix-nt.html.  I had already read this document when it
was posted to the list this summer.  If you have not read the document,
take ten minutes and do so.  It is well done and should help in any attempt
by management to force NT into your domain.

Thanks

