From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Sep 09 09:53:20 1998
From: Peter.Braack () degussa ! de
Date: Wed, 09 Sep 1998 09:53:20 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: LSM: import failed
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078721911720

Dear admins,

I wrote:
last night one member of a ASE-cluster crashed. The remaining node trie=
d to
start the service (Oracle database) and failed (reasons still not clear=
).
Hosts: 2x Alpha 2100, DU 4.0B with patch 7, ASE 1.41
Right now we have both members up and the diskgroup is deported, all di=
sks
offline.
I can set the disks online and can read the configuration with voldisk =
list
<disk>. Everythinks seems fine, disklabels are ok, too.
However, voldg import dgname AND voldg -f import dgname failed with "Di=
sk group
has no valid configuration copies".
Digital CSG has no further ideas and we're running out of time. Do you =
have any
ideas how to import that diskgroup?
We'll start to restore the backup soon, but that is going to take some =
time...

I recived on reply (thanks to Felix Maurer).

The solution came from Digital CSC:
LSM Metadata of that diskgroup were corrupt.
Fortunately, we run volsave each night and the metadata is stored by th=
at tool
(.../dgname.d/dgname.DF)
We created a new diskgroup named dg2 with an empty disk, added all disk=
s from
the original diskgroup and restored the metadata.
This procedure is described in the LSM Manual, Section C.13.
In short:

# voldg init dg2 rze84=3Drze84
# voldisk online rza81
# voldisk online rz...
...
# voldg -g dg2 adddisk rza81=3Drza81
# voldg -g dg2 adddisk rz...
....
# volmake -g dg2 -d p11dbdg.DF

After that, all volumes must be startet and the Advfs-Domains have to b=
e
created by hand
(Modify existing links or create dir in /etc/fdmns and create links to =
volumes
in /dev/vol )

Oracle is up and running again!

Peter
Peter.Braack@degussa.de
