Thanks to responses from Sean O'Connell and Randall Winchester I was able
to put in place a new, sendmail-891 customized "mailstats" binary file.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

My question:--

On Tue, 8 Sep 1998, Deen Ipaye wrote:

> 
> Dear Sendmail gurus:
> 
> After a previous/botched attempt to install sendmail.8.8.8,
> I finally went for sendmail.8.9.1  (with much thanks to Paul Youngblood
> who provided invaluable pointers).
> 
> After the instal,  I am getting the following error message when I 
> issue the "mailstats" command--
> 
> "mailstats: file size has changed"
> 
> Looks like the format of the "sendmail.st" changed from the previous
> version under sendmail-5.65
> 
> My question is--  how do I modify the format so "mailstats" would work?
> 
> Thanks in anticipation; a summary will be posted
> 
> -Deen
> 
> 

How it was resolved:

[A]
I went to the "mailstats" directory in my sendmail 8.9.1 install path.
It contains lots of "mailstats*" files plus a "Build" command.
I executed the "./Build"  and it created an obj. sub-directory,
"obj.OSF1.V4.0.alpha."

I then "cd" to this new directory and voila, it contains a new "mailstats"
binary.   I copied it to "/usr/sbin/mailstats" after renaming the old one
with a ".old" appendage (in case I want to go back to it).

Thanks Sean, for being the spark plug!  (-;

[B]
As per Randall Winchester...

> Make sure you are running the new mailstats program that comes with
> sendmail-8.9.1, then "cp /dev/null sendmail.st" from what ever directory
> you keep the sendmail.st file in.
>
> There is new information being kept in the sendmail.st file now, 
> including number of rejects and number of discards.
>

...Done &  *THANKS* guys!

-Deen

