------ 
Thanks for everyone who replied:

John Nebel <nebel@athena.csdco.com>
Martin Mokrejs <mmokrejs@natur.cuni.cz>
Ian Mortimer <ian@physics.uq.edu.au>
------
Ian Mortimer pointed out that follows:

This could be due to the DNS security bug which affects versions of 
BIND prior to 4.9.7 which means the one shipped with DU 4.0b.

If that's so then someone is attempting to exploit this vulnerability
to break into your system.  The good news is that DU's version of
named just dies and dumps core so they won't succeed in breaking
in that way.

The solution is to upgrade to either BIND 4.9.7 or BIND 8.1.2.
The first is the easiest quick fix because it's compatible with 
the version shipped with DU (4.9.3).

You can get BIND from 

   http://www.isc.org/bind.html

Your sendmail problems most likely result from the nameserver
crash.
-------
Best Regards,
