The DEC C++ is on the Associated Products Vol #1 cd.

Following info from Tom Webster with many saying the same thing:


The binaries are linked against the C++ runtime libraries.  Unfortunately,
DEC changed the setld name of the CXXRTL that the installer is looking for
between the time the utility was written and it was released.

1. Make sure you have the current CXXRTL installed off of the Comp Products CD.


2. Copy the install directory for the management utilites to a disk and edit
   the installer script to look for the correct name of the C++ runtime libs.
   You can find what is installed using "setld -i | grep -i CXX".

